{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>אֶת כָּל שְׂעָרוֹ</b> (all his hair) — A general term, then a specification, then again a general term, to include every place of gathering of visible hair; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 14:9). But in the Sifra (Torat Kohanim, chapter 2:2:3): \"And he shall shave אֶת שְׂעָרוֹ\" — one might think even the hidden places, therefore Scripture says \"גַּבּוֹת עֵינָיו\" (his eyebrows); just as גַּבּוֹת עֵינָיו are visible, so too all his hair must be visible — this excludes the hidden places. If from גַּבּוֹת עֵינָיו, which are a place of gathering of visible hair, we learn so too every place of gathering of visible hair, then from where do we derive gathering of hair in what is not visible, and scattered hair in what is not visible? Scripture says \"אֶת כָּל שְׂעָרוֹ יְגַלֵּחַ\" (all his hair he shall shave).\n\nBut the Rav (Maimonides) held by the midrash of Rabbi Yishmael: what does it include? — the hair of the legs; and what does it exclude? — the underarms (דְּבֵית הַשֶּׁחִי) and the entire body (דְּכוּלֵּי גּוּפֵהּ). But here the halakhah is that he shaves everything (כִּדְלַעַת), whether because the halakhah follows the midrash, or because the halakhah follows the opinion of Rabbi Akiva, for the Rav [holds] the entire body, except for that which is inside the nose alone. And so we learned in our Mishnah (Negaim 14:2): \"And he passed a razor over all his flesh,\" and it is explained in the second chapter of Sotah (16a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:53.805929569Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}